{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_584702223#4_1380514589","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains the mechanism: heavy BOJ buying of JGBs raises bond prices and forces down yields; the BOJ implemented yield-curve control in 2016 to keep 10-year JGB yields at zero. This is direct evidence for why Japanese bond yields/market rates dropped after 2010.","learned":"Heavy BOJ purchases increased demand for JGBs, raised their prices, and forced yields down; YCC was introduced in 2016 to keep the 10-year JGB yield at zero."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ jgb \"japanese government bond\") (+ liquidity trading market) (+ decline declined dropping dried) (+ \"bank of japan\" boj purchases))","reason":"Explore the alternative interpretation that the user means the Japanese bond market's activity/liquidity has been dropping since 2010, especially due to BOJ purchases absorbing supply."}}
