{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1610995300#0_3271820615","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage is related to BOJ monetary easing, negative rates, asset purchases, and JGB yield-curve effects, but it is mainly a 2016 market note about future policy speculation and does not directly explain why the Japanese bond market or JGB yields have been dropping since 2010.","learned":"BOJ policy debate in 2016 included deeper negative rates versus more asset purchases, with concerns about limits to JGB buying and effects on the JGB yield curve."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"japanese government bond\" jgb) (+ \"record low\" \"all-time low\" negative) (+ yield yields) (+ \"bank of japan\" boj) (+ easing deflation))","reason":"Search for documents discussing JGB yields hitting record lows or negative levels and attributing the decline to BOJ easing and deflation, likely to provide direct evidence for the post-2010 drop."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"japanese government bond\" jgb) (+ \"record low\" \"all-time low\" negative) (+ yield yields) (+ \"bank of japan\" boj) (+ easing deflation))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_106621170#0_202788333","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3003","rank":4,"snippet":"term interest rate unchanged at -0.1% and maintained the target for the 10-year <cover>Japanese government bond yield at around 0% during its April meeting, as widely expected. In a quarterly outlook report, the central bank slashed its consumer inflation forecast for the current fiscal year to 0.1% from earlier predictions made in January of 0.5%, amid downward pressure on service spending. Policymakers also warned of lingering risks to the economic outlook as the COVID-19 pandemic continues to hurt consumption. Meantime, the projected rates of rise in the GDP for the current fiscal year were little changed (4% vs 3.9% made in January). The central bank reaffirmed it would not hesitate to take additional easing measures if necessary. In 2020, the BoJ eased monetary policy twice, mostly by expanding asset-buying and creating a new facility to deliver funds via financial institutions to companies hit by a coronavirus. source: Bank of Japan Interest Rate in Japan averaged 2.41 percent from 1972 until 2021, reaching an all time high of 9 percent in December of 1973 and a record low </cover>of -0.10 percent in January of 2016. This page provides - Japan Interest Rate - actual ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1610995300#0_3271820615","rank":1,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1053083924#1_2120551809","rank":2,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_1289489410#9_2747135624","rank":3,"relevance":2}]}}
