{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ abenomics kuroda \"monetary easing\") (+ \"government bond\" \"government bonds\" jgb) (+ \"bank of japan\" boj) (+ yield yields purchases))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_691818304#8_1616422691","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3027","rank":1,"snippet":"dubbed \"The Night of the Long Knives \". ON THIS DAY NISS agents interrogated Younes on an article where he predicted a bloody purge (a Night of the Long Knives) within the National Congress Party, as he referred to a power struggle among the different factions of the ruling party. Sudan's security apparatus ban journalists from reporting Shinzo Abe is mired in a political scandal and yet another LDP factional night of the long knives. The path to 110, a target I outlined a month ago, was inevitable given US Treasury-<cover>JGB yield spreads, Fed-BoJ monetary tightening timetables and the political time bomb that now haunts Abenomics. </cover>King Dollar's safe-haven surge has only just begun The bean counters conspired in a night of the long knives to remove one their most respected coaching talents and Wotte was also forced to fall on his sword. SFA make things right by bringing back boss Billy This brings us back to the night of the long knives:\" , \"start_char\": 3571.000000 , \"title\": \"Night of the long knives - Idioms by The Free Dictionary\" , \"url\":"}}
