{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1108199124#7_2334744163","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage is from a Japan-focused article on lowflation and BOJ policy. It directly supports the explanation for suppressed Japanese bond yields: weak demand keeps inflation very low, the BOJ missed its 2% inflation target, and it pledged to keep interest rates extremely low for an extended period, reinforcing a zero/negative JGB-yield environment.","learned":"Japan's demand-deficient lowflation trap led the BOJ to keep interest rates extremely low for an extended period, helping keep JGB yields near zero or negative."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3041","reason":"This result list is still producing strong Japan-focused evidence about low inflation, BOJ QE, and extremely low interest rates suppressing Japanese bond yields; continue while budget remains."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3041"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1108199124#8_2334745840","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3041","rank":5,"snippet":"\"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1108199124#8_2334745840\" , \"end_char\": 4968.000000 , \"headings\": \"Japan's Lowflation Problem May 30, 2021,05:30pm EDT Brazil’s Hit Bottom. But Maybe Not Bolsonaro. Japan's Lowflation Problem \" , \"segment\": \"The Bank of Japan admitted that raising inflation to the 2% policy target was taking much longer than it expected. But the <cover>Bank of Japan is not throwing in the towel just yet. Yesterday, it pledged to keep interest rates at their current “extremely low” levels for “an extended period of time.” Interestingly, it also threw a sop to banks struggling to make profits in a very low </cover>interest rate environment: it cut the excess reserve balance on which negative interest is paid, effectively allowing banks to hold more reserves interest-free. Perhaps most importantly, the Bank of Japan reaffirmed its commitment to QE: It will continue expanding the monetary base until the year-on-year rate of increase in the observed CPI (all items less fresh food) exceeds 2 percent and stays above the target in a stable manner. So it will be QE "}}
