{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1108199124#8_2334745840","relevance":3,"reason":"This Japan-focused Forbes passage directly supports the explanation for suppressed Japanese bond yields: the BOJ acknowledged inflation was taking longer than expected to reach 2%, pledged to keep interest rates extremely low for an extended period, and reaffirmed continued QE until inflation sustainably exceeded target.","learned":"BOJ's failure to reach its 2% inflation target led it to maintain extremely low rates and continue QE, reinforcing near-zero or negative JGB yields."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3041","reason":"The q3041 result list continues to produce grade-3 Japan-focused evidence about low inflation, BOJ QE, and extremely low rates suppressing Japanese bond yields; continue while remaining judgment budget allows."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3041"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2785955681#3_3079826620","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3041","rank":6,"snippet":"is that foreign exchange rates may change in such a way that the investor would have to pay back more expensive currency with less valuable currency. In theory, according to uncovered interest rate parity, carry trades should not yield a predictable profit because the difference in interest rates between two countries should equal the rate at which investors expect the low-interest-rate currency to rise against the high-interest-rate one. However, carry trades weaken the currency that is borrowed, because investors sell the borrowed money by converting it to other currencies. By early year 2007, it was estimated that some US$1 trillion may have been staked on the yen carry trade. Since the mid-1990s, the <cover>Bank of Japan has set Japanese interest rates at very low </cover>levels making it profitable to borrow Japanese yen to fund activities in other currencies. These activities include subprime lending in the USA, and funding of emerging markets, especially BRIC countries and resource rich countries.\" , \"start_char\": 1931.000000 , \"title\": \"Carry (investment) - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carry_(investment)\" }"}}
